# CR 703.4g: human's precombat main phase starts with a d6 roll to visit
# Attractions, since human controls one (PhaseHandler.java:292-295). The
# scenario seed rolls a light Ferris Wheel shows (Lights:4 5 6), so it is
# visited, and Motion Sickness's "whenever you visit an Attraction" (Mode$
# VisitAttraction, ValidCard$ Attraction.YouCtrl) moves the Aura to the other
# tapped creature. Both creatures have protection from artifacts, so Ferris
# Wheel's own Visit trigger has no legal target and is removed (CR 603.3d):
# its phase-out Effect would sit in the command zone, which a fixture cannot
# load back (GameState.java:225-233 writes it by a name no card has).
startturn human
queue optionaltrigger true
queue targets 4
advance 3
resolvestack
